<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000/T December fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000/T December fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of fuel oil for loading in December, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 3.0-percent sulphur grade fuel oil cargo is to be lifted from Kaohsiung between December 15-27 or December 23-27.</p>
<p>The tender will close November 18 and is valid until November 19.</p>
<p>CPC last sold a high sulphur fuel oil cargo for November 14-18 loading to a western trader at close to $120 per tonne on free-on baord Kaohsiung basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703082).</p>
</text>
